include g474.tdc
diagram h-slow "Thread → thread, slow mode (79 %): two SysTick reprograms in the switch"
letter "H slow"
new
num value "1957 cycles"
num share "79 %"
num path "k_sem, giver (prio 2) → taker (prio 1)"
num arch "PendSV (USE_SWITCH=n)"
what "The same path as the fast mode, but here the giver's slice timeout is the first timeout. Its abort programs SysTick for the next timeout, and the add of the taker's slice timeout programs it again. About a third of the thread to thread time is these two reprograms. They move the next interrupt by some microseconds out of 20 ms. The dashed cursor shows where the fast mode ends (card H fast)."
evidence "ISR → giver has one reprogram: 1263 against 1570 cycles (307). Giver → taker has two: 680 cycles."
evidence "Mean t2t: sem 1812, fifo 1862, wakeup 1877, msgq 1934, mutex 2042, event 2149, poll 2150 cycles."
evidence "The driver core skips a reprogram to the same deadline tick (timer_core_arm(), drivers/timer/system_timer_generic.h:531-534), but the abort between the two adds moves the deadline first."
src "thread-baseline-1m/20261029T021724Z"

axis "cycles after the give call" -100..2050

taker pending -100.. "blocked in k_sem_take()" : The taker waits in k_sem_take() with K_FOREVER.

at -100
giver  100 : The giver was woken by the stimulus ISR.
@give
@fast ref "fast mode" at give+1277
giver  300 "k_sem_give()" : The giver gives the semaphore. The taker has a higher priority, so update_cache() selects it as the next thread.
giver  310? "slice reset" : The same slice reset as in the fast mode (card H fast). The split is not measured.
@r0 anchor
giver  340 "reprogram 1" : z_try_abort_timeout() of the giver's slice timeout. It was the first timeout, so the driver programs SysTick for the next one (kernel/timeout.c:239-250).
giver  340 "reprogram 2" : z_add_timeout() of the taker's slice timeout. It is the first timeout again, so the driver programs SysTick again (kernel/timeout.c:225-233).
@r1 anchor
giver  121 "z_swap()" : The giver pends PendSV and unlocks (arch_swap(), arch/arm/include/cortex_m/kernel_arch_func.h:84-105).
hw     12 : Exception entry into PendSV.
@pendsv anchor
pendsv 447 "switch giver → taker" : z_arm_pendsv: save the giver, take the taker from the ready queue cache (with BASEPRI), restore the taker.
taker  87 : The taker returns from k_sem_take() and reads TIM2->CNT.
@runs "taker runs"
giver  pending runs..2050 "preempted" : The giver is ready, but the taker has the higher priority.

mask 40..1411 "BASEPRI" : Scheduler lock and timeout lock.
mask pendsv+20..pendsv+50? "BASEPRI" : z_arm_pendsv sets BASEPRI at swap_helper.S:123 and restores the BASEPRI of the taker (0) at swap_helper.S:270, before the MPU reprogram (bl z_arm_configure_dynamic_mpu_regions, :305). The length is not measured: an estimate from the number of instructions.

span give..runs "1957, measured" !
span r0..r1 "680, measured as the distance of the modes" !
